Description: Implements a Bayesian hierarchical model for differential prevalence 
    analysis, tailored for microbiome studies. The method accommodates both 
    cross-sectional and longitudinal designs, providing finite effect estimates 
    and uncertainty intervals that are naturally adjusted for multiple testing 
    via hierarchical shrinkage. Posterior inference is performed via Markov 
    chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) using 'cmdstanr' as the backend.
